arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App for a logistics company. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-882b56d2f78f4dc1adc391b98c3682bf/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. It uses .NET 11 preview, SQLite, ASP.NET Core Identity.

The project structure:
- `ShipmentTracker/` — server project (hosts app, EF Core, Identity, API endpoints)
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` — client project (all interactive UI components go here)
- Solution file: `ShipmentTracker.sln`

**IMPORTANT Auto mode rules:**
- All interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project
- Components cannot access DbContext directly — use HTTP APIs
- Both Program.cs files must register matching services
- No `@rendermode` needed on pages (global mode is already configured in App.razor)

## What to Build

### 1. Shared Models (in Client project under `Models/`)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentStatus.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string SenderName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public double WeightKg { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/CreateShipmentRequest.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class CreateShipmentRequest
{
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string RecipientName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string SenderName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public double WeightKg { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in Client project under `Services/`)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsAsync(ShipmentStatus? statusFilter = null);
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(CreateShipmentRequest request);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus);
}
```

### 3. Client-side HTTP Implementation (in Client project)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetShipmentsAsync(ShipmentStatus? statusFilter = null)
    {
        var url = "/api/shipments";
        if (statusFilter.HasValue)
            url += $"?status={statusFilter.Value}";
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>(url) ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        try
        {
            return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>($"/api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        }
        catch (HttpRequestException ex) when (ex.StatusCode == System.Net.HttpStatusCode.NotFound)
        {
            return null;
        }
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(CreateShipmentRequest request)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PostAsJsonAsync("/api/shipments", request);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"/api/shipments/{id}/status", new { Status = newStatus });
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
    }
}
```

### 4. Register HttpClient and services in Client Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp =>
